{sections.map((s,i)=><><section id={s.id}><h2>{s.title}</h2>{s.paragraphs.map(p=><p>{p}</p>)}</section>{i<3 && <AdSlot id={`article-0${i+2}-middle`} kind="article"/>}</>)}
<section aria-label="Related historical guide"><h2>Historical context: what is a gaucho?</h2><p>Readers exploring <em>gaucho meaning</em> often begin by asking <em>what is a gaucho</em>. The answer involves work, mobility, law, and literature as well as traditions; see our <a href="/en/what-is-a-gaucho/">historical introduction to the gaucho</a> for that wider context.</p></section>
<section id="references"><h2>Sources and editorial method</h2><p>These notes expand the research and vocabulary of our Spanish cultural guide for an English-speaking audience. Historical claims, literary representations and modern editorial images are distinguished. External documents remain with their original custodians.</p><ul>{sources.map(s=><li><a href={s.url} target={s.url.startsWith('https:')?'_blank':undefined} rel={s.url.startsWith('https:')?'noopener noreferrer':undefined}>{s.name}</a></li>)}</ul>
<p><a href="/en/magazine/">← Return to the English cultural magazine</a> · <a href="/en/what-is-martin-fierro/">An introduction to Martín Fierro</a></p></section>
